  "note": "A ridge line parallel to the LOC: its top is the key, held at all cost, all round with a bias to the front; the forward spurs occupied for strength and depth, the infiltration routes between the side spurs covered (MW s12 para 13 p 157). A and B Coys on the top, D Coy the reserve on the top behind them; C Coy on the forward spurs. Strong points with all round defence, at least a Pl strong point in each Coy posn on its most dominating feature with 30 days' staying power; tiers from the foothills or valleys to the ridge, the final battle on the ridge (MW s12 paras 8-9 p 152). Frontage on IBB's extended row (MW prints no figure).",
